---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const phases = [
  { n: '01', name: 'Launch', body: 'A small, contained start. One process, one pipeline, no disruption to anything running today.' },
  { n: '02', name: 'Interpret', body: 'The intelligence layer begins reading what your existing systems already produce. You start seeing your business without changing how it runs.' },
  { n: '03', name: 'Understand', body: 'A full operational audit. What happens, who does it, where the time goes, and what the vendor stack really costs.' },
  { n: '04', name: 'Replace', body: 'The layer starts doing work instead of only watching it. Legacy tools become optional one function at a time.' },
  { n: '05', name: 'Own', body: 'You operate through an AI-native interface. The old vendor contract becomes an archive, not a dependency.' },
];
---
<Layout title="Paul Ann Labs - AI Deployed Inside the Business">
  <section class="relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden bg-navy text-cream lg:block">
    <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-5 pt-6 pb-14 sm:pt-10 sm:pb-16 lg:py-32">
      <div class="flex max-w-xl flex-col lg:block lg:max-w-lg xl:max-w-xl">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-fig">Paul Ann Labs</p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 text-4xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-5xl text-balance">
        What would it mean to walk in already knowing what happened?
      </h1>
      <p class="order-last mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-light lg:order-none">
        Not a dashboard. Not another subscription. An intelligence layer that reads what
        your business already produces ... then quietly grows until the systems you're
        stuck with stop mattering.
      </p>
      <a href="/methodology/#phase-one"
         class="mt-9 self-start inline-block rounded bg-fig px-8 py-3 font-semibold text-navy hover:bg-fig-light transition-colors">
        See how Phase One works
      </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="relative order-first h-56 sm:h-80 lg:order-none lg:absolute lg:inset-y-0 lg:right-0 lg:left-[40%] lg:h-full">
      <picture>
      <source media="(max-width: 1023px)" srcset="/media/hero-pal-r2-phone.webp" width="865" height="569" />
      <img
        src="/media/hero-pal-r2-desk.webp"
        alt="An open service bay lit from inside at blue hour, with a pickup and workers"
        width="1896"
        height="630"
        fetchpriority="high"
        class="h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
      </picture>
      <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-10 lg:hidden" style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(26,47,61,0) 0%, rgba(26,47,61,1) 100%)"></div>
      <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 hidden lg:block" style="background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(26,47,61,1) 0%, rgba(26,47,61,0.6) 18%, rgba(26,47,61,0) 40%)"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-20">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Nobody rips out their systems</h2>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-slate">
      Every AI proposal a small business gets asks them to replace something that works.
      Migrate the data, retrain the staff, sign a new contract, pray. Most owners say no,
      and they're right to.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate">
      The strangler fig doesn't fight the tree. It grows around it, gradually, until one
      day the fig is holding itself up and the tree is just history inside it. That's the
      shape of this. Nothing gets torn out. The layer grows until removal isn't a decision
      anyone has to make.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-navy/10 bg-white py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Five phases</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-slate">
        Each one earns the next. Most engagements stop somewhere in the middle, and that's
        a legitimate place to stop.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 space-y-5">
        {phases.map(p => (
          <div class="flex gap-6 rounded-lg border border-navy/10 bg-cream p-6">
            <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-fig-ink">{p.n}</span>
            <div>
              <p class="font-semibold text-navy">{p.name}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate">{p.body}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <a href="/methodology/" class="mt-8 inline-block font-semibold text-fig-ink hover:underline">
        How the methodology works &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-20">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">The part most AI projects skip</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-slate">
      Software doesn't fail because the model was wrong. It fails because nobody inside
      the company owned it.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-navy/10 bg-white p-7">
        <p class="font-semibold text-navy">Stems</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate">
          We find the person already inside your company who should be running this ...
          usually not the one with the title. They become the owner, not us.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href="/peppermint/" class="rounded-lg border border-navy/10 bg-white p-7 hover:border-fig transition-colors">
        <p class="font-semibold text-navy">Peppermint</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate">
          A reskilling program for the people already on payroll. Not a seminar ...
          a curriculum that moves a team up the automation curve.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-fig-ink">See the program &rarr;</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="bg-navy-deep py-20 text-cream">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">Start with Phase One.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-light">
        One process. One month. If the intelligence layer doesn't show you something you
        didn't already know, there's no reason to continue ... and we'll say so first.
      </p>
      <a href="mailto:john@yourlastcorporatejob.com?subject=Paul%20Ann%20Labs%20inquiry"
         class="mt-8 inline-block rounded bg-fig px-8 py-3 font-semibold text-navy hover:bg-fig-light transition-colors">
        john@yourlastcorporatejob.com
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
